{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the life of Sarah was a hundred years and twenty years and seven years.</b> Therefore שָׁנָה is written for each and every total, to tell you that each one is expounded on its own: at a hundred she was like a twenty-year-old for sinning — just as a twenty-year-old has not sinned, since she is not one subject to punishment, so too at a hundred, without sin; and at twenty she was like a seven-year-old for beauty." "<b>The years of Sarah's life.</b> All of them were equal for good."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:00.391712208Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}